# E-COMMERCE SOVEREIGNTY: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> Consolidates `ecommerce.mdc`. One rule, absolute authority on all commerce logic.

## 1. TRANSACTIONAL INTEGRITY — Zero-Trust Pricing
- **Server-Only**: Frontend NEVER calculates final price. PaymentIntent amount = server-side DB read only.
- **No Negatives**: Final price MUST invoke `Math.max(0, total)` before PaymentIntent creation.
- **Client Data**: Ignore ALL price/amount from client. Recalculate server-side every time.

## 2. STRIPE MANDATES
```typescript
// ✅ Webhook verification — FIRST line of any webhook handler
const event = stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(
  request.rawBody, signature, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.value()
);

// ✅ Idempotency check — BEFORE any processing
const processed = await db.collection('webhook_events').doc(event.id).get();
if (processed.exists) return response.status(200).send('Already processed');
```
- **Secret**: `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` via `defineSecret()`. NEVER `.env`.
- **Double-billing**: Forbidden. Check `event.id` in Firestore before every webhook action.

## 3. INVENTORY — Atomic Transactions
```typescript
// ✅ Atomic stock decrement
await db.runTransaction(async (t) => {
  const doc = await t.get(productRef);
  const newStock = doc.data().stock - quantity;
  if (newStock < 0) throw new Error('OUT_OF_STOCK');
  t.update(productRef, { stock: newStock });
});
```
- **Never** use plain `update()` for stock. Always `runTransaction()`.
- If stock < 0: throw immediately, never allow negative inventory.

## 4. CHECKOUT UX RULES (Rule 19 Enforcement)
- Checkout buttons MUST survive Z-index traps on mobile — no `backdrop-blur` parent clipping.
- Playwright E2E tests MUST use `{ force: true }` locators for checkout CTA confirmation.
- Post-purchase flow (receipt + confirmation email) runs synchronously — assume user kills tab immediately after payment.

## 5. ADMIN SOVEREIGNTY (RBAC)
- All inventory/product/order mutations: `admin: true` custom claim verified server-side.
- Client-side UI gating is insufficient — always back-check with Firebase Auth custom claims.
- Order lifecycle: `Pending → Processing → Shipped → Delivered/Refunded` with Tracking ID injection.
- Never mutate historical invoice data when updating prices — use `draft` vs `active` separation.

## 6. SECURITY
- Firestore rules MUST assert `quantity > 0` and `price >= 0` on all cart writes.
- App Check enforced on all checkout callable functions.
